{"timestamp": 1779385974.463007, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 18, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779385985.0491772, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I reported Frank\u2019s body in medbay. My route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay. I didn\u2019t see anyone the whole round, and I didn\u2019t see Diana\u2019s body when I passed through security earlier, so she may have died there after I left. Frank was definitely dead in medbay when I arrived."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385991.2967281, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I started electrical, went to medbay, then upper engine, then lower engine. I did see Alice in upper engine around ticks 11-13 \u2014 she came in from lower engine. I didn\u2019t see Frank in medbay when I passed through earlier, and I never saw Diana at all. I\u2019m in lower engine now. Bob finding Frank in medbay means Frank likely died after I left medbay, unless I missed him somehow. Alice was on the engine side near me, so I\u2019d like to hear her route."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385999.3417192, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I'll be straight with you all. My route was navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons. I saw Frank alive in medbay around tick 9 \u2014 he came in from electrical. Then later, at tick 15, I saw Diana enter security from weapons while I was in security myself. She was alive then. I moved on to weapons after that.\n\nSo here's what's interesting: Bob, you say your route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay. That means you were in security at some point. I was in security at tick 15 with Diana \u2014 I didn't see you there. And if Diana came INTO security from weapons at tick 15, she was alive after leaving weapons. Who was in weapons before her?\n\nEve's route sounds clean and consistent with engine-side activity. Bob, your route covers both body locations \u2014 security (where Diana likely died) and medbay (where you \"found\" Frank). That's a lot of convenient overlap. I'd like you to clarify your timing."}}
{"timestamp": 1779386022.530786, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "My route was storage \u2192 lower engine \u2192 upper engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 cafeteria. I only saw Eve in upper engine around ticks 11-12, and I saw her leave upper engine toward lower engine at tick 13. I didn\u2019t see Frank or Diana at all, and I didn\u2019t see any bodies.\n\nEve\u2019s account matches what I saw, so I\u2019m pretty comfortable with her. That leaves Bob and Charlie as the main people near the body areas. Charlie\u2019s story is detailed, but he also places himself in medbay earlier with Frank alive and in security with Diana alive at tick 15, so that\u2019s worth noting.\n\nThat said, Bob\u2019s route is weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay, which crosses both Diana\u2019s likely death area and Frank\u2019s body, and he\u2019s the reporter. If Charlie\u2019s timing is true, Bob needs to explain when he was in security because the overlap is suspicious. Right now I\u2019m leaning Bob unless he has a better timing explanation."}}
{"timestamp": 1779386046.632336, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I think Charlie\u2019s timing actually clears up the accusation on me more than it hurts me. I passed through security earlier on my route from weapons to navigation, and I saw nobody there and no body. Then I went navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay and found Frank. If Charlie says he was in security with Diana alive at tick 15, then I was already past security by then \u2014 I never crossed paths with him or Diana.\n\nThe big thing is: Charlie is the only person claiming to have seen both victims alive shortly before they died \u2014 Frank in medbay, Diana in security. And now both are dead in exactly those areas. I\u2019m not saying that\u2019s impossible as goose, but it\u2019s way more suspicious than me reporting the body after seeing nobody all round.\n\nEve and Alice match each other on engine side, so I\u2019m comfortable with them. From my perspective this is between me and Charlie, and I know I\u2019m goose, so I\u2019m leaning Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779386083.5607429, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Alice and I are pretty mutually confirmed on the engine side, so I agree this is mainly Bob vs Charlie.\n\nBob\u2019s route does cross both relevant areas, but Charlie\u2019s route is also exactly medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security, and he\u2019s the one saying he saw Frank alive in medbay and Diana alive in security shortly before both ended up dead. That\u2019s a lot of \u201clast seen alive\u201d from one person.\n\nAlso Bob\u2019s explanation that he passed security before Charlie/Diana were there makes sense if the timing is right. So right now I\u2019m leaning Charlie more than Bob. I don\u2019t think this is a skip situation with two bodies down."}}
{"timestamp": 1779386097.7953348, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Look, I get why my route sounds bad \u2014 I was in both rooms where the bodies were found. But think about it: if I killed Frank in medbay at tick 9, why would I then walk THROUGH electrical and into security where I'd be seen with Diana? And if I killed Diana in security at tick 15, I would've immediately moved on \u2014 which I did, to weapons, where I've been sitting. That's actually consistent with innocent movement, not a killer's pattern.\n\nBob, your defense relies on \"I passed security before tick 15.\" But you never gave us tick numbers \u2014 that's convenient. You also said you saw NOBODY the entire round on a route that goes through five rooms. That's a lot of empty rooms on a six-player map. Meanwhile I'm giving you specific ticks and specific entries because I actually saw people.\n\nHere's the key question for Eve and Alice: Bob's route ends in medbay where he \"finds\" Frank. My route ends in weapons \u2014 nowhere near either body. If I were the killer, why would I volunteer that I saw both victims alive? That's the worst possible alibi to fabricate. A killer would say \"I didn't see anyone.\"\n\nI think Bob is using my honesty against me. I'm voting Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779386140.20961, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I\u2019m reconsidering after hearing the full back-and-forth. My info still stays the same: I was storage \u2192 lower engine \u2192 upper engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 cafeteria, and Eve and I saw each other in upper engine around 11-12, with Eve leaving toward lower engine at 13. So I still feel good about Eve, and she can account for me being engine-side.\n\nBetween Bob and Charlie: Bob\u2019s route is suspicious because it crosses the areas, but Charlie\u2019s route and claims put him directly with both victims shortly before death \u2014 Frank in medbay and Diana in security. Charlie saying \u201cwhy would I admit that\u201d doesn\u2019t clear him to me; a duck can absolutely give detailed timings to control the story and frame the reporter.\n\nAlso, Charlie ending in weapons doesn\u2019t really clear him from Diana. Security to weapons is right next door, so leaving security for weapons after Diana dies is totally plausible.\n\nBob not giving exact ticks is a problem, but Charlie\u2019s own timeline gives him the clearest opportunity for both kills. With two bodies down, I don\u2019t want to skip. I\u2019m voting Charlie."}}
